{# Gotenberg's own running footer for the wiki export - a COMPLETE, standalone document, which is
   what Chromium expects of a footer template. Modelled on
   templates/progression/_qualiopi_footer.html.twig, whose three hard-won constraints hold here too:

   - it inherits NOTHING from index.html - no stylesheet, no font, no variable - so everything it
     needs is written here, inline;
   - Chromium renders it with a font-size of zero unless one is stated, and clips it to the page's
     bottom margin, so that margin (see App\Service\WikiPdfExporter) must be tall enough for it;
   - a TABLE at an EXPLICIT width, not flexbox at 100%: Chromium ignores `display: flex` here and
     concatenates the cells, and a percentage resolves against something wider than the printable
     area, cutting the right-hand cell off mid-word. 186mm is A4's 210mm less the two 12mm side
     margins - this number and the exporter's margins move together.

   `pageNumber` and `totalPages` are Chromium's own classes, filled at print time. #}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="fr">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<style>
    body { margin: 0; font-family: 'Source Sans 3', 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif;
           font-size: 7.5pt; color: #6b7688; -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact; print-color-adjust: exact; }
    table.f { width: 186mm; margin: 0 auto; border-collapse: collapse; border-top: 0.5pt solid #d3dae4; }
    table.f td { padding-top: 1.2mm; }
    .f__mid { color: #8a93a3; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<table class="f">
    <tr>
        <td align="left">{{ documentTitle }}</td>
        <td align="center" class="f__mid">page <span class="pageNumber"></span>/<span class="totalPages"></span></td>
        <td align="right">Édité le {{ generatedAt|date('d/m/Y') }} · MonCampus</td>
    </tr>
</table>
</body>
</html>
